From cf780b1ec12857cc813bdd0ffc9bcb3e0d05dbd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Belkin <anton.belkin@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:56:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mac/common: show the sample buffer layer's HDR frames with
 EDR, or as SDR

Since macOS 26 a layer's preferredDynamicRange defaults to standard, so
macOS tone mapped the layer's HLG and PQ frames to SDR on HDR displays
too. Ask for high (wantsExtendedDynamicRangeContent before macOS 26),
and add --macos-sample-buffer-edr=no for SDR on any display: with a
Dolby Vision RPU, its trims for SDR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../macos-sample-buffer-layer.txt             |  1 +
 DOCS/man/options.rst                          |  5 +++++
 osdep/mac/app_bridge.h                        |  1 +
 osdep/mac/app_bridge.m                        |  2 ++
 video/out/mac/common.swift                    |  2 ++
 video/out/mac_common.swift                    | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/DOCS/interface-changes/macos-sample-buffer-layer.txt b/DOCS/interface-changes/macos-sample-buffer-layer.txt
